1
00:00:05,970 --> 00:00:10,970
Ben Franklin once said, by failing to prepare, you are preparing to fail.
本·富兰克林曾经说过：不做准备，就是在准备失败。

2
00:00:10,970 --> 00:00:14,970
It's vital that you prepare for each lab activity.
为每一项实验活动做好准备是至关重要的。

3
00:00:14,970 --> 00:00:17,970
Before you begin, determine the possible risks,
开始之前，先确定可能存在的风险，

4
00:00:17,970 --> 00:00:21,970
wear the right PPE, and be aware of any protective measures
穿戴合适的个人防护装备，并了解所有防护措施

5
00:00:21,970 --> 00:00:25,970
and emergency responses that are pertinent for the chemicals that you'll be working with.
以及与你将要使用的化学品相关的应急处置方法。

6
00:00:25,970 --> 00:00:31,970
When diluting acids or bases, always add the acid or the base to the solvent,
稀释酸或碱时，一定要把酸或碱加入溶剂中，

7
00:00:31,970 --> 00:00:34,970
such as water, not the other way around.
比如水，而不是反过来。

8
00:00:34,970 --> 00:00:38,970
Pouring the solvent into an acid or base can cause a violent reaction,
把溶剂倒入酸或碱中可能会引起剧烈反应，

9
00:00:38,970 --> 00:00:40,970
and you may get burned.
你可能会被烧伤。

10
00:00:40,970 --> 00:00:42,970
Never remove chemicals from the lab.
绝不要把化学品带出实验室。

11
00:00:42,970 --> 00:00:48,970
Use a brake-resistant secondary container to transport chemicals between lab spaces.
在不同实验室空间之间转移化学品时，要使用防破碎的二次容器。

12
00:00:48,970 --> 00:00:54,970
Chemicals must be handled safely in order to avoid skin, eye, or inhalation exposure.
必须安全地处理化学品，以避免皮肤、眼睛接触或吸入暴露。

13
00:00:54,970 --> 00:00:57,970
First, let's talk about protecting your eyes.
首先，我们来谈谈如何保护眼睛。

14
00:00:57,970 --> 00:01:00,970
As we mentioned in our lesson about PPE,
正如我们在个人防护装备那一课中提到的，

15
00:01:00,970 --> 00:01:03,970
safety glasses with side shields offer some protection,
带侧护罩的安全眼镜能提供一定的防护，

16
00:01:03,970 --> 00:01:07,970
but they won't help you when working with a potential splash hazard.
但在有潜在飞溅危险的操作中，它们帮不了你。

17
00:01:07,970 --> 00:01:11,970
Splash goggles are more effective at protecting your eyes.
防溅护目镜保护眼睛的效果更好。

18
00:01:11,970 --> 00:01:17,970
Chemical splash goggles should be marked with the code Z87.1.
化学防溅护目镜上应标有代码 Z87.1。

19
00:01:17,970 --> 00:01:23,970
This code indicates compliance with American National Standards Institute.
这个代码表示符合美国国家标准学会的标准。

20
00:01:23,970 --> 00:01:26,970
Prescription glasses don't offer adequate eye protection.
处方眼镜不能提供足够的眼部防护。

21
00:01:26,970 --> 00:01:28,970
Wear safety glasses.
要戴安全眼镜、

22
00:01:28,970 --> 00:01:32,970
Goggles or a full face shield over your prescription glasses.
护目镜或全面罩，戴在你的处方眼镜外面。

23
00:01:32,970 --> 00:01:37,970
Corrosive chemicals will harm you if they splash or come into contact with your skin.
腐蚀性化学品一旦飞溅或接触到皮肤就会伤害你。

24
00:01:37,970 --> 00:01:41,970
A lab coat and gloves will help protect your skin to a degree,
实验服和手套能在一定程度上保护你的皮肤，

25
00:01:41,970 --> 00:01:48,970
but a full-length chemical-resistant lab apron is the best choice when working with splash hazards.
但在有飞溅危险的操作中，全长的耐化学品实验围裙是最好的选择。

26
00:01:48,970 --> 00:01:51,970
If you're working with an especially corrosive chemical,
如果你使用的是腐蚀性特别强的化学品，

27
00:01:51,970 --> 00:01:56,970
use full arm-length rubber gloves instead of the typical nitro gloves.
要使用长及整条手臂的橡胶手套，而不是普通的丁腈手套。

28
00:01:56,970 --> 00:02:00,970
Some chemicals in the lab can harm you without even touching you.
实验室里有些化学品甚至不用接触你就能伤害你。

29
00:02:00,970 --> 00:02:04,970
That's why it's important to be aware of inhalation exposure.
这就是为什么要注意吸入暴露。

30
00:02:04,970 --> 00:02:06,970
Never smell chemicals.
绝不要去闻化学品。

31
00:02:06,970 --> 00:02:09,970
Always work with toxic chemicals under a fume hood,
处理有毒化学品时一定要在通风柜内操作，

32
00:02:09,970 --> 00:02:13,970
and keep containers closed tightly if you're not using them.
不使用时要把容器盖紧。

33
00:02:13,970 --> 00:02:19,970
If a large chemical spill occurs, evacuate, seal off the lab, and notify the authorities.
如果发生大量化学品泄漏，要撤离、封锁实验室，并通知有关部门。

34
00:02:19,970 --> 00:02:22,970
Large spills can produce excessive vapors.
大量泄漏会产生过多的蒸气。

35
00:02:22,970 --> 00:02:25,970
They have to be cleaned by qualified personnel.
必须由合格的人员来清理。

36
00:02:25,970 --> 00:02:30,970
Don't re-enter the lab until your supervisor gives you the all clear.
在主管宣布解除警报之前，不要重新进入实验室。

37
00:02:30,970 --> 00:02:33,970
Flammable chemicals require special handling techniques.
易燃化学品需要特殊的处理方法。

38
00:02:33,970 --> 00:02:39,970
First, always know the flammability and explosive potential for each chemical you're working with.
首先，一定要了解你所使用的每种化学品的易燃性和爆炸可能性。

39
00:02:39,970 --> 00:02:45,970
Keep flammables away from all ignition sources, such as bunts and burners or hot plays.
让易燃物远离所有点火源，比如本生灯或加热板。

40
00:02:45,970 --> 00:02:50,970
Store flammable chemicals in a dedicated and grounded storage cabinet.
把易燃化学品存放在专用且接地的储存柜中。

41
00:02:50,970 --> 00:02:55,970
When you're finished working in the lab, properly dispose of chemicals and waste
在实验室工作结束后，要按照联邦、州、地方和机构的要求，

42
00:02:55,970 --> 00:03:00,970
according to federal, state, local, and institutional requirements.
妥善处置化学品和废弃物。

43
00:03:00,970 --> 00:03:05,970
Use chemical-resistant plastic or metal containers for waste disposal.
使用耐化学品的塑料或金属容器来处置废弃物。

44
00:03:05,970 --> 00:03:10,970
Solvent should never be evaporated under a fume hood as a means of disposal.
绝不应通过在通风柜中蒸发溶剂的方式来处置它们。

45
00:03:10,970 --> 00:03:14,970
Check with your lab supervisor for the best way to evaporate solvents.
请向你的实验室主管咨询蒸发溶剂的最佳方法。

46
00:03:14,970 --> 00:03:19,970
Any materials used to clean up a chemical spill, such as paper towels,
用于清理化学品泄漏的任何材料，比如纸巾，

47
00:03:19,970 --> 00:03:24,970
are also considered hazardous waste and must also be disposed of accordingly.
也被视为危险废物，同样必须按相应规定处置。

48
00:03:24,970 --> 00:03:29,970
Preparation is the key to handling chemicals safely in the lab.
做好准备是在实验室安全处理化学品的关键。

49
00:03:29,970 --> 00:03:35,970
Know what you're working with, how to handle it, and what to do in case of accidental exposure.
要知道你在用什么、如何处理它，以及发生意外暴露时该怎么做。

50
00:03:35,970 --> 00:03:41,970
In our next lesson, we'll talk about a few other common lab hazards that you need to prepare for.
在下一课中，我们将讨论你需要做好准备应对的其他几种常见实验室危害。
